/T (Social, Humanitarian and Cultural Committee \(SOCHUM\) is the third committee of the United Nations General Assembly. Established in 1945, its primary mandate is to address global human rights violations, social development, and humanitarian affairs.This Committee discusses questions relating to the advancement of women, the protection of children, indigenous issues, the treatment of refugees, the promotion of fundamental freedoms through the elimination of racism and racial discrimination, and the right to self-determination among many other issues.)
/E (Social, Humanitarian and Cultural Committee \(SOCHUM\) is the third committee of the United Nations General Assembly. Established in 1945, its primary mandate is to address global human rights violations, social development, and humanitarian affairs.This Committee discusses questions relating to the advancement of women, the protection of children, indigenous issues, the treatment of refugees, the promotion of fundamental freedoms through the elimination of racism and racial discrimination, and the right to self-determination among many other issues.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
