/T (Social factors play a crucial role in shaping youth mental health outcomes. Family relationships, peer interactions, socioeconomic conditions, exposure to violence, and discrimination can either protect or harm well-being. The expansion of digital platforms has created both opportunities and risks. While social media can raise awareness and build supportive communities, it can also contribute to cyberbullying, social comparison, and excessive screen use, increasing risks of anxiety and depression.)
/E (Social factors play a crucial role in shaping youth mental health outcomes. Family relationships, peer interactions, socioeconomic conditions, exposure to violence, and discrimination can either protect or harm well-being. The expansion of digital platforms has created both opportunities and risks. While social media can raise awareness and build supportive communities, it can also contribute to cyberbullying, social comparison, and excessive screen use, increasing risks of anxiety and depression.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
